From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: balance shared package resource lifetime

QCA8084 package probe acquires clocks and an exclusive reset without
releasing them on failure or removal. The PCS/XPCS helpers also attach
devres to sibling MDIO devices, whose lifetime does not follow the PHY
probe. A deferred or failed PHY probe can therefore leave those resources
claimed. Conversely, package_remove_once releases shared PCS/XPCS handles
on the first PHY removal while other package members can still use them.

Serialize package acquisition and count successful users. Register each
user's release after joining the package and before acquiring per-PHY
resources, so devres releases per-PHY clocks before the package handles
and frees the shared storage last. Release all partial acquisitions on
failure, and release the complete package only after its final user.

Manage PCS/XPCS allocations and their clock, reset and MDIO references
explicitly with the package. Validate channel indices before storing
resources, and unwind every acquired channel on error. Track the PCS and
channel clock enables owned by this driver, avoiding duplicate enables
on repeated speed notifications and balancing them at final teardown.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
